---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import WidgetLoader from '../../../../components/WidgetLoader.astro';
---
<Layout>
  <article class="topic-page">
    <span class="level-badge">Foundational</span>
    <h1>Linear Functions</h1>
    <p>Straight-line relationships: <code>y = m·x + c</code>. Slope <code>m</code> is steepness; <code>c</code> is where the line crosses the y-axis.</p>

    <section>
      <h2>Concept</h2>
      <p>Double <code>m</code> and the line gets twice as steep. Change <code>c</code> and the whole line slides up or down. Try it below.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Interactive plotter — y = m·x + c</h2>
      <div class="widget" id="line-widget">
        <WidgetLoader widgets={['plotter']} />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Slider lab — slope and intercept</h2>
      <div class="widget" id="slope-widget">
        <WidgetLoader widgets={['sliderLab']} />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Step-by-step — finding slope from two points</h2>
      <div class="widget" id="slope-steps">
        <WidgetLoader widgets={['equationStep']} />
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
